From 53c324faac3bb7311bb633662b7b057db0fb4a4e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Roscoe <bryanroscoe@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 21:04:53 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 23/30] Tokens: Furygale Flocking's flyers all get flying and
 haste
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Furygale Flocking: "For each opponent, create two 3/3 blue and red
Elemental creature tokens with flying that attack that opponent this turn
if able. They gain haste until end of turn."

- Parser (token.rs): the keyword list after "with" stops at a relative
  clause (" that …"), which describes the tokens' behaviour, not more
  keywords. The whole "flying that attack that opponent this turn if
  able" had failed to parse as a keyword, so the tokens had no flying.
- CR 608.2c: "They" names every token the repeated instruction made.
  The repeat loop ran the token creation once per opponent and the
  following haste instruction once after it, reading only the last
  iteration's tokens; it now publishes every token the loop created.

Not done: "attack that opponent this turn if able" is still not
enforced (the clause stays flagged by the swallowed-clause check).

Tests: token.rs keyword_clause_stops_at_a_relative_clause;
tests/integration/furygale_flocking_tokens_per_opponent.rs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
